readme_b35 = '''- **B35/A36 v2 preregistration is FROZEN PRE-OUTCOME and the finite DEVELOPMENT replay implementation is on PR #69 for exact-head acceptance.** The original `atlas-b35-a36-conditional-evidence-v1-pre-outcome` fingerprint `7bfd1cfdd65e946d45caa99dd2a35a90d8b424cb82cad5941ad26cac51816c4c` is preserved as **superseded pre-outcome lineage**; no B35 outcomes were opened under it. Before any outcome access, the control review corrected two preregistration defects without changing B34: a B34 bar stamped 11:30 ET is information-safe at 11:31 ET, and a raw prior-close/current-open gap that crosses an overnight split is `UNAVAILABLE` for non-gap condition profiling rather than invalidating an otherwise same-session ORB/premarket/HVD signal. The active contract is `atlas-b35-a36-conditional-evidence-v2-pre-outcome-clock-split-corrected` with fingerprint `145cc8983439b6062fd5e60303539d1611cdf7db0119ed68a7da1e68ffd8eda6`; B34 remains bound unchanged at `6f7239fcda11ac6c890d2635980d431ec49e346707d9cc549f111bd50daaa4bf`. The final signal-time bucket is `1031_TO_1131`, and 20-return realized volatility requires 21 completed closes in one split epoch.\n- **The B35 finite DEVELOPMENT replay implementation is deliberately restartable, compact, and authority-limited.** It binds exact expected minute units to the immutable native acquisition-plan `year/month/batch/unit` identity, confines checkpoint/canonical/split artifacts to the isolated V2 roots without symlink escape, lazily verifies canonical SHA-256 before open, validates raw/unadjusted physical rows and strict Boolean adjustment schema, and rejects a mutated in-memory plan whose content no longer matches its fingerprint. A self-hash DEVELOPMENT authorization is published under an exclusive claim before outcomes; replay output is serialized, a self-hash outcome-read-start marker survives a failed authorized replay, completed symbol-batch outputs use self-hash receipts and restart-safe orphan handling, and the final run binds validated receipt identities. Entry delay is measured from the information-safe decision, exact target opens resolve at the target before later intrabar ambiguity, short returns/costs use entry notional, and entered-but-unresolved opportunities retain their attempted exposure evidence. The faster fired-setup scan only prefilters candidate bars and delegates final signal truth to the unchanged B34 evaluators. No giant permanent minute-feature lake is created. PIT market-regime context remains `UNAVAILABLE` when an exact accepted prior-session join is unavailable rather than guessed. Short signals may be profiled as RESEARCH evidence, but A34 portfolio admission remains long-only until borrow/locate/recall economics are accepted.\n- **PR #69 implementation acceptance itself has opened no B35 historical outcomes.** For this package, consumed-master rows read = `0`, future-blind rows read = `0`, provider calls = `0`, broker reads = `0`, broker writes = `0`, PAPER orders = `0`, LIVE operations = `0`; strategy promotion = `false`, selector promotion = `false`, PAPER authority is unchanged/absent, and LIVE authority remains `false`. DEVELOPMENT scored outcomes still end `2026-04-30`; the consumed `2026-05-12..2026-08-11` master interval is never reusable; the new blind starts on/after `2026-09-08` and remains unopened. This implementation does not complete the conditional selector evidence. After exact-head acceptance/merge, the sequence is workstation `--source-only` preflight → control review → explicit `--authorize-development-outcomes` → frozen DEVELOPMENT strategy × condition evidence → walk-forward selector/profile evidence → later one-time future-blind evaluation after sufficient accrual.\n'''
